          "ruleId": "CWE-798",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Hardcoded default JWT secret enables authentication bypass and role forgery in local auth mode\n\nWhen `JWT_SECRET` is not set in the environment, the backend falls back to a hardcoded, publicly-known default secret (`super-agent-local-dev-secret-change-in-production`) with no startup guard. In local auth mode, any attacker who can reach the API can forge a valid JWT authenticating as any user with any role (including `owner`) and any organization ID."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
