          "ruleId": "CWE-346",
          "ruleIndex": 2,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Internal service token HMAC uses public Cognito userPoolId as secret, enabling unauthenticated token forgery in cognito mode\n\nWhen `AUTH_MODE=cognito`, internal service tokens are HMAC-signed with the Cognito `userPoolId` — a public identifier that the backend itself returns on the unauthenticated `GET /api/auth/config` endpoint. Any attacker who can read that endpoint can forge internal tokens authenticating as any user with any role, bypassing profile and membership lookups entirely."
          },
          "locations": [
