          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "9.8",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "f56f36e4813f00dbee7160658df0916e62f38b85266f3b44051ba304aac2940c",
            "synthetic_location": true,
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0003",
              "severity": "critical",
              "cvss": 9.8,
              "timestamp": "2026-11-20 13:18:02 UTC",
              "target": "/workspace/agentcore-superagent-update/super-agent/backend",
              "cwe": "CWE-346",
              "impact": "In cognito mode, full authentication bypass as an arbitrary identity/role/org with no database lookups, on every route protected by `authenticate`. The same primitive is what agent subprocesses legitimately use, so the bypass is indistinguishable from a trusted internal caller.",
              "technical_analysis": "`src/middleware/auth.ts:79-80` sets the internal token HMAC key: `const INTERNAL_TOKEN_SECRET = config.authMode === 'cognito' ? config.cognito.userPoolId : config.jwtSecret;`. The `userPoolId` is not a secret — `src/routes/auth.routes.ts:29-40` (`GET /api/auth/config`, registered unauthenticated in `src/routes/index.ts`) returns `userPoolId` (and clientId, region, domain) to any caller in cognito mode, since the frontend needs it.\n\n`verifyInternalToken` (`auth.ts:94-108`) only recomputes `HMAC-SHA256(userPoolId, data)` and compares, then `authenticate` (`auth.ts:160-171`) installs the payload's `sub/email/orgId/role` directly as `request.user` **before any Cognito verification or profile/membership lookup** — the internal-token branch returns early. So in cognito mode the entire authorization decision can rest on a value the server publishes to anonymous users.",
              "remediation_steps": "Use a dedicated, operator-provided high-entropy secret (independent of JWT_SECRET and of any Cognito identifier) as the internal token HMAC key, loaded from the environment with no default. Long term, prefer an asymmetric scheme so the API only holds a public key.",
              "counterevidence": "Only reachable in cognito mode (AUTH_MODE=cognito); in local mode the HMAC key is config.jwtSecret which is not disclosed by /auth/config. Default auth mode is 'local', so deployments using the default mode are not exposed to this specific path. Could not test against a live deployed instance (out of scope for this run).",
              "confidence": "high",
              "severity_change_conditions": "Confirmation that a production deployment runs in cognito mode would confirm critical; evidence that no cognito-mode deployment exists would lower practical severity though the code flaw remains.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Fetch `GET /api/auth/config` (unauthenticated) and read `userPoolId`.\n2. Build payload `{sub, email, orgId, role: 'owner', exp: now+3600}`, base64url-encode it, HMAC-SHA256 it with the `userPoolId`, and assemble `internal.<data>.<sig>`.\n3. Send it as a Bearer token to any authenticated route — `authenticate` accepts it before any Cognito or profile verification.\n4. Executed as a vitest test against the real `src/middleware/auth.ts` in cognito mode with mocked Prisma; token accepted, `req.user` set to the forged claims, `role: owner`.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
